thcare”[Title/Abstract] OR “Access to health care”[Title/Abstract] OR"},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "database_search", fact_id: "8040f64ddabe", section: "trang-85", evidence: "Database Search \"Healthcare service* availability\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Health care service* availability\"[Title/ Abstract] OR \"Healthcare access\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Health care access\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Health economic indicator*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Productivity loss\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Budget impact\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Absenteeism\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Economic evaluation\"[Title/ Abstract] OR \"Cost of diabetes\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Socioeconomic disparit*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Health equity\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Socioeconomic factor*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Socioeconomic factor*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Social determinant* of health\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Prevention strateg*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Risk management strateg*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Risk factor management\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Risk factor reduction\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Selfmanagement strateg*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Modifiable risk behavi*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Behavioral determinant*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Behavioural determinant*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Behavioral risk*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Behavioural risk*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Healthcare professional engagement*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Health professional engagement*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Public health impact*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Health policy effectiveness\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Policy impact metric*\"[Title/Abstract] ) ) OR ( ( \"Diabetes Evaluation\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Diabetes Mellitus Evaluation\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Diabetes Surveillance\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Diabetes Mellitus Surveillance\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Diabetes Monitoring\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Diabetes Mellitus Monitoring\"[Title/Abstract] ) AND ( \"Indicator*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Benchmark*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Metric*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Index\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Indices\"[Title/Abstract] ) ) ) AND ( \"Consensus\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Framework*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Review*\"[Title/Abstract] OR \"Delphi\"[Title/Abstract] )"},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "care_metric", fact_id: "89716c13c731", section: "trang-91", evidence: "Benchmarks”)) OR (ti:(“Care Metric”) OR ti:(“Care Metrics”)) OR (ab:(“Care Metric”) OR ab:(“Care Metrics”)) OR (ti:(“Care Index”)) OR (ab:(“Care Index”)) OR (ti:(“Care Indices”)) OR (ab:(“Care Indices”)) OR (ti:(“Health System Indicator”) OR ti:(“Health System Indicators”)) OR (ab:(“Health System Indicator”) OR ab:(“Health System Indicators”)) OR (ti:(“Health System Benchmark”) OR ti:(“Health System Benchmarks”)) OR (ab:(“Health System Benchmark”) OR ab:(“Health System Benchmarks”)) OR (ti:(“Health System Metric”) OR ti:(“Health System Metrics”)) OR (ab:(“Health System Metric”) OR ab:(“Health System Metrics”)) OR (ti:(“Health System Index”)) OR (ab:(“Health System Index”)) OR (ti:(“Health System Indices”)) OR (ab:(“Health System Indices”)) OR (ti:(“Health Facility Indicator”) OR ti:(“Health Facility Indicators”)) OR (ab:(“Health Facility Indicator”) OR ab:(“Health Facility Indicators”)) OR (ti:(“Health Facility Benchmark”) OR ti:(“Health Facility Benchmarks”)) OR (ab:(“Health Facility Benchmark”) OR ab:(“Health Facility Benchmarks”)) OR (ti:(“Health Facility Metric”) OR ti:(“Health Facility Metrics”)) OR (ab:(“Health Facility Metric”) OR ab:(“Health Facility Metrics”)) OR (ti:(“Health Facility Index”)) OR (ab:(“Health Facility Index”)) OR (ti:(“Health Facility Indices”)) OR (ab:(“Health Facility Indices”)) OR (ti:(“Monitoring framework”) OR ti:(“Monitoring frameworks”)) OR (ab:(“Monitoring framework”) OR ab:(“Monitoring frameworks”))"},
    {a: "type_2_diabetes", b: "noncommunicable_disease_facility_based_monitoring_guidance", fact_id: "578bb9565617", section: "trang-69", evidence: "Noncommunicable disease facility-based monitoring guidance: framework, indicators and application (https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/364379)."},
    {a: "type_2_diabetes", b: "hearts_d", fact_id: "ab2bf180f164", section: "trang-69", evidence: "HEARTS-D: diagnosis and management of type 2 diabetes. Geneva: World Health Organization; 2020 (https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/331710)."},
    {a: "type_2_diabetes", b: "who_discussion_paper", fact_id: "6438d65863dd", section: "trang-69", evidence: "WHO discussion paper. Geneva: World Health Organization; 2021 (https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/who-discussion-paper-draft-recommendationsto-strengthen-and-monitor-diabetes-responses-within-nationalnoncommunicable-disease-programmes-including-potential-targets, accessed 26 May 2024)."},
    {a: "criteria", b: "technical_expert_meeting", fact_id: "ec359fa2fb9c", section: "trang-13", evidence: "collectability; and ease of interpretation and use. These criteria were presented to the expert panel during an introductory technical expert meeting held on 25 October 2023, prior to the survey launch."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "framework", fact_id: "7b78d00d0762", section: "trang-13", evidence: "those which did not meet the threshold for retention in the framework but did receive acceptable validity and feasibility ratings), and to clarify ambiguous or conflicting feedback on indicator metadata in order to finalize the framework."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "national_diabetes_prevention_and_control_plan", fact_id: "8f86d5aa4833", section: "trang-30", evidence: "Existence and implementation of national diabetes prevention and control plan Purpose To assess the availability of governance mechanisms for diabetes prevention and control at national level."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "medicines_and_health_products_price_survey", fact_id: "781c6d104cae", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Some indicators may be generated from other sources, such as medicines and health products price survey (40), logistics information system, health workforce information system, national health insurance claims database, poverty assessments (national statistics office reports) (41), and population census."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "logistics_information_system", fact_id: "93bcce3883f7", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Some indicators may be generated from other sources, such as medicines and health products price survey (40), logistics information system, health workforce information system, national health insurance claims database, poverty assessments (national statistics office reports) (41), and population census."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "health_workforce_information_system", fact_id: "49b8ca2f1fcf", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Some indicators may be generated from other sources, such as medicines and health products price survey (40), logistics information system, health workforce information system, national health insurance claims database, poverty assessments (national statistics office reports) (41), and population census."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "national_health_insurance_claims_database", fact_id: "2f2d6609b83d", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Some indicators may be generated from other sources, such as medicines and health products price survey (40), logistics information system, health workforce information system, national health insurance claims database, poverty assessments (national statistics office reports) (41), and population census."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "poverty_assessments_national_statistics_office_reports", fact_id: "2504b3840b58", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Some indicators may be generated from other sources, such as medicines and health products price survey (40), logistics information system, health workforce information system, national health insurance claims database, poverty assessments (national statistics office reports) (41), and population census."},
    {a: "diabetes_prevention_and_control", b: "population_census", fact_id: "7039b1d130e9", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Some indicators may be generated from other sources, such as medicines and health products price survey (40), logistics information system, health workforce information system, national health insurance claims database, poverty assessments (national statistics office reports) (41), and population census."},
    {a: "overweight_and_obesity", b: "overweight_and_obesity_assessment", fact_id: "97fe54fe0a6d", section: "trang-45", evidence: "Purpose To assess the level of overweight and obesity assessment in health facilities."},
    {a: "hypertension", b: "blood_pressure_control", fact_id: "a454f1659e48", section: "trang-22", evidence: "u Blood pressure control"},
    {a: "diabetes_complications", b: "assessment_of_risk_factor_for_diabetes_complications", fact_id: "4af6d8586f15", section: "trang-19", evidence: "Processes of care: diagnosis, assessment of risk factor for diabetes complications and assessment of complications"},
    {a: "retinopathy", b: "retinopathy_treatment", fact_id: "d7bad2376fa2", section: "trang-59", evidence: "Definition Proportion of people with diabetes and retinopathy who received retinopathy treatment based on guidelines."},
    {a: "chronic_kidney_disease", b: "urine_albumin_to_creatinine_ratio_acr", fact_id: "5264c40a41bd", section: "trang-53", evidence: "Urinary albumin excretion can be estimated in a spot urine sample using several tests (from most preferred to least preferred): ● urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio (ACR) ● urine protein-to-creatinine ratio (PCR) ● reagent strip (“dipstick”) urine analysis for albumin or total protein with automated reading ● reagent strip (“dipstick”) urine analysis for albumin or total protein with manual reading."},
    {a: "chronic_kidney_disease", b: "urine_protein_to_creatinine_ratio_pcr", fact_id: "9dc45ca314c3", section: "trang-53", evidence: "Urinary albumin excretion can be estimated in a spot urine sample using several tests (from most preferred to least preferred): ● urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio (ACR) ● urine protein-to-creatinine ratio (PCR) ● reagent strip (“dipstick”) urine analysis for albumin or total protein with automated reading ● reagent strip (“dipstick”) urine analysis for albumin or total protein with manual reading."},
    {a: "overweight", b: "nationally_or_sub_nationally_representative_population_based_surveys", fact_id: "0824ed57b361", section: "trang-63", evidence: "Sources of data Nationally or sub-nationally representative population-based surveys with height and weight measurement."},
    {a: "overweight", b: "height_and_weight_measurement", fact_id: "33c35c767c56", section: "trang-63", evidence: "Sources of data Nationally or sub-nationally representative population-based surveys with height and weight measurement."},
    {a: "overweight", b: "age_standardization", fact_id: "4457d3c61184", section: "trang-63", evidence: "Limitations/comments For any comparison over time or with other populations, age standardization is needed. Method of assessment of overweight and obesity may vary in countries."},
    {a: "overweight", b: "method_of_assessment_of_overweight_and_obesity", fact_id: "b279bfeee780", section: "trang-63", evidence: "Limitations/comments For any comparison over time or with other populations, age standardization is needed. Method of assessment of overweight and obesity may vary in countries."},
    {a: "overweight", b: "bmi__test", fact_id: "37a112194d1f", section: "trang-63", evidence: "4 BMI = weight (kg)/height (m)2."},
    {a: "glycaemic_control", b: "population_based_survey", fact_id: "1a5110cbd9b5", section: "trang-68", evidence: "This indicator can be derived from population-based surveys or health facility-based routine data."},
    {a: "glycaemic_control", b: "clinical_target", fact_id: "8b3e6badc50b", section: "trang-68", evidence: "Based on WHO guidelines: Clinical target: <126 mg/dl (7 mmol/l) Global target: <178 mg/dl (9.9 mmol/l)"},
    {a: "glycaemic_control", b: "national_targets_and_guidelines", fact_id: "51700934ba12", section: "trang-66", evidence: "● Glycaemic control can be alternatively defined in accordance with national targets and guidelines."},
    {a: "glycaemic_control", b: "hba1c_measurement", fact_id: "14a1243c0635", section: "trang-66", evidence: "Sources of data Nationally or sub-nationally representative population-based surveys, with HbA1c measurement, health facility patient registers, health records."},
    {a: "ncds_including_diabetes", b: "ncd_country_capacity_survey", fact_id: "85190018c929", section: "trang-24", evidence: "Data collection frequency of key data sources Key data source Data collection frequency NCD country capacity survey and other surveys Every 2 years Health facility survey Every 3 to 5 years Routine facility reporting system Continuous Population-based survey Every 3 to 5 years CRVS Continuous NCD country capacity survey The NCD country capacity survey (26) is a global survey on national capacity for NCD prevention and control that is conducted regularly by WHO. This enables Member States and the global community to monitor progress and achievements in improving their capacities in responding to the epidemic of NCDs including diabetes. NCD country focal points respond to a standard online questionnaire depicting various aspects on health system infrastructure, financing, governance, surveillance, primary health care, partnerships and collaborations, specific to NCDs. It has been conducted in 2001, 2005, 2010 and biennially since 2013 and with 193 countries participating in the most recently conducted survey in 2023 (31)."},
    {a: "ncds", b: "ncd_country_capacity_survey", fact_id: "947eaabb713e", section: "trang-24", evidence: "Data collection frequency of key data sources Key data source Data collection frequency NCD country capacity survey and other surveys Every 2 years Health facility survey Every 3 to 5 years Routine facility reporting system Continuous Population-based survey Every 3 to 5 years CRVS Continuous NCD country capacity survey The NCD country capacity survey (26) is a global survey on national capacity for NCD prevention and control that is conducted regularly by WHO. This enables Member States and the global community to monitor progress and achievements in improving their capacities in responding to the epidemic of NCDs including diabetes. NCD country focal points respond to a standard online questionnaire depicting various aspects on health system infrastructure, financing, governance, surveillance, primary health care, partnerships and collaborations, specific to NCDs. It has been conducted in 2001, 2005, 2010 and biennially since 2013 and with 193 countries participating in the most recently conducted survey in 2023 (31)."},
    {a: "ncds", b: "routine_facility_reporting_system", fact_id: "ddf51be7be46", section: "trang-24", evidence: "The Noncommunicable disease facility-based monitoring guidance (16) provides indicator standards and an approach for improving routine facility reporting systems with person-level monitoring, for assessing service delivery for NCDs including diabetes in primary care settings."},
    {a: "ncds", b: "patient_monitoring_systems", fact_id: "685f20e540a1", section: "trang-24", evidence: "Patient monitoring systems are important for capturing aggregate facility-based statistics for NCDs."},
    {a: "ncds", b: "individual_level_data", fact_id: "2a8027710921", section: "trang-24", evidence: "In the 2021 NCD country capacity survey (31), about 55% of countries reported collecting individual-level data on NCDs in primary health centres, using paper-based, electronic or mixed systems, with the majority of electronic systems more prevalent in highincome countries."},
    {a: "disease_risk_factors", b: "population_based_survey", fact_id: "7924b25e275e", section: "trang-25", evidence: "Population-based surveys are important for measuring disease risk factors and other social determinants that cannot be generated reliably from routine facility reporting systems (34)."},
    {a: "method_of_estimation_country", b: "evidence_based_national_guidelines", fact_id: "1d8681035a77", section: "trang-33", evidence: "Existence of evidence-based national guidelines, protocols, standards or technical guidance is validated by examining documents that outline the scientific steps that were taken to develop the national guidelines, protocol, standards or technical guidance."},
    {a: "diabetes_management", b: "referral_and_back_referral_system_for_diabetes_management", fact_id: "2b7dbe313eba", section: "trang-34", evidence: "Definition The country has a clearly defined and well-established functional referral and back-referral system for diabetes management, facilitating the seamless transition between primary care, secondary and tertiary care."},
    {a: "diabetes_management", b: "referral_system", fact_id: "5a4a08554cab", section: "trang-34", evidence: "Existence of a clearly defined, well-established functional referral system is validated by examining documents that outline mechanisms for referral from primary care to secondary and tertiary care, as well as feedback mechanisms from higher to lower levels of care."},
    {a: "insulin_delivery_devices", b: "national_health_benefit_package", fact_id: "14c618a10d27", section: "trang-35", evidence: "The indicator is considered “Yes” if the country has a national health benefit package that includes insulin, insulin delivery devices and blood glucose self-monitoring."},
    {a: "blood_glucose_self_monitoring", b: "national_health_benefit_package", fact_id: "6468e8f61d68", section: "trang-35", evidence: "The indicator is considered “Yes” if the country has a national health benefit package that includes insulin, insulin delivery devices and blood glucose self-monitoring."},
    {a: "noncommunicable_disease", b: "harmonized_health_facility_assessment_hhfa", fact_id: "eb04f7fb3684", section: "trang-39", evidence: "Related links Harmonized health facility assessment (HHFA): comprehensive guide. Geneva: World Health Organization; 2022 (https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/365534)."},
    {a: "diabetes_programme_management", b: "diabetes_surveillance_system", fact_id: "c3068a0f12e9", section: "trang-42", evidence: "Indicator name Availability and quality of a diabetes surveillance system Purpose To assess the availability of quality and comprehensive surveillance data for diabetes programme management."},
    {a: "cardiovascular_disease_risk", b: "cardiovascular_disease_risk_assessment", fact_id: "8e4e27bc0aa1", section: "trang-47", evidence: "Purpose To assess the level of cardiovascular disease risk assessment among people aged 40 years and over in health facilities."},
    {a: "probability_of_death_between_exact_age_30_and_exact_age_70", b: "standard_life_table_methods", fact_id: "53fd977e549a", section: "trang-80", evidence: "Method of estimation Probability of death between exact age 30 and exact age 70 are calculated using cause-specific mortality rates in each 5-year age group and standard life table methods."},
    {a: "probability_of_death_between_exact_age_30_and_exact_age_70", b: "who_global_health_estimates_ghe", fact_id: "e3dff6f66eef", section: "trang-80", evidence: "The estimates are derived from the WHO Global health estimates (GHE)."},
    {a: "probability_of_death_between_exact_age_30_and_exact_age_70", b: "crosscountry_comparability", fact_id: "59631d21dca3", section: "trang-80", evidence: "These estimates represent the best estimates of WHO, computed using standard categories, definitions and methods to ensure crosscountry comparability, and may not be the same as official national estimates."},
    {a: "probability_of_death_between_exact_age_30_and_exact_age_70", b: "stratify_by_type_of_diabetes", fact_id: "fd53f90aa676", section: "trang-80", evidence: "Disaggregation Where possible and applicable, stratify by type of diabetes, individual characteristics such as age, sex, race/ethnicity, comorbidity status, highrisk groups, socioeconomic status, residence type (urban/rural), and health insurance type."},
    {a: "probability_of_death_between_exact_age_30_and_exact_age_70", b: "civil_registration_with_complete_coverage_and_medical_certif_581d53", fact_id: "d4bdaf8588a2", section: "trang-80", evidence: "Sources of data Civil registration with complete coverage and medical certification of cause of death."},
    {a: "diabetes_mellitus", b: "who_mortality_database", fact_id: "68b90e45eb9f", section: "trang-84", evidence: "WHO Mortality database: Diabetes mellitus [Online database]. Geneva: World Health Organization; "},
    {a: "diabetes_mellitus", b: "civil_registration_and_vital_statistics", fact_id: "6cbd2d5ba20c", section: "trang-84", evidence: "www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/civil-registration-and-vital-statistics, accessed 26 May 2024)."}
  ] AS row
  MATCH (a:DiabetesConcept {id: row.a})
  MATCH (b:DiabetesConcept {id: row.b})
  MERGE (a)-[r:DIAGNOSED_BY {source_id: source.id, fact_id: row.fact_id}]->(b)
  SET r += row, r.a = null, r.b = null, r.fact_id = row.fact_id
  RETURN count(*) AS rel_count_1
}
CALL {
  WITH source
  UNWIND [
    {a: "diabetes", b: "elevated_blood_glucose_levels", fact_id: "2dadb6693ce8", section: "trang-13", evidence: "Diabetes is a chronic condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels due to inadequate insulin production by the pancreas or the body’s inability to properly utilize the insulin it produces."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "good_control_of_glycaemia", fact_id: "b34e52ae3043", section: "trang-21", evidence: "● 80% of people with diagnosed diabetes have good control of glycaemia."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "good_control_of_blood_pressure", fact_id: "fc92a7f40012", section: "trang-21", evidence: "● 80% of people with diagnosed diabetes have good control of blood pressure."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "morbidity", fact_id: "72411a104db2", section: "trang-22", evidence: "This domain assesses the results of interventions and the overall performance of the health system in the prevention and control of diabetes, including morbidity, hospitalization and mortality associated with diabetes and complications such as cardiovascular diseases."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "hospitalization", fact_id: "e8b941bdbe7f", section: "trang-22", evidence: "This domain assesses the results of interventions and the overall performance of the health system in the prevention and control of diabetes, including morbidity, hospitalization and mortality associated with diabetes and complications such as cardiovascular diseases."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "mortality", fact_id: "e39055b901f4", section: "trang-22", evidence: "This domain assesses the results of interventions and the overall performance of the health system in the prevention and control of diabetes, including morbidity, hospitalization and mortality associated with diabetes and complications such as cardiovascular diseases."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "raised_blood_glucose", fact_id: "bbcd86978773", section: "trang-72", evidence: "Raised blood glucose criteria: ● FPG ≥ 126 mg/dl (7 mmol/L); or ● HbA1c ≥ 6.5% (48 mmol/mol)."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "affordable", fact_id: "88b1a835177e", section: "trang-36", evidence: "Method of estimation The indicator is considered “Yes”, that is, affordable, if: [(NPL +monthly cost for insulin, insulin devices and blood glucose selfmonitoring to person with diabetes) /LPGW wage] ≤1"},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "lower_extremity_amputation", fact_id: "50764c9741c5", section: "trang-77", evidence: "Definition Proportion of people with diabetes who had a lower-extremity amputation."},
    {a: "type_2_diabetes", b: "insulin_resistance", fact_id: "523f2bbfc2a1", section: "trang-13", evidence: "Type 2 diabetes occurs most commonly in adults and is characterized by insulin resistance and some insulin deficiency."},
    {a: "gestational_diabetes", b: "blood_glucose_values_above_normal", fact_id: "c6bd86162b04", section: "trang-13", evidence: "Gestational diabetes occurs in pregnancy with blood glucose values above normal but below those that are characteristic of diabetes."},
    {a: "chronic_kidney_disease", b: "estimated_glomerular_filtration_rate_egfr_of_60ml_min_per_1_73m2", fact_id: "64bf372f6ba7", section: "trang-53", evidence: "Definition The proportion of people with diabetes registered in health facilities who were assessed for diabetic kidney disease based on the following criteria: ● Presence of an estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) of <60mL/min per 1.73m2 on at least two occasions, 1 to 3 months apart; and/or ● Presence of albuminuria in at least two urine samples, 1 to 3 months apart."},
    {a: "chronic_kidney_disease", b: "albuminuria", fact_id: "91f000ab3a6a", section: "trang-53", evidence: "Definition The proportion of people with diabetes registered in health facilities who were assessed for diabetic kidney disease based on the following criteria: ● Presence of an estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) of <60mL/min per 1.73m2 on at least two occasions, 1 to 3 months apart; and/or ● Presence of albuminuria in at least two urine samples, 1 to 3 months apart."},
    {a: "glycaemic_control", b: "good_control_of_glycaemia", fact_id: "0cef97ff2ae2", section: "trang-66", evidence: "Definition Proportion of people living with diabetes with good glycaemic control based on HbA1c measurement."}
  ] AS row
  MATCH (a:DiabetesConcept {id: row.a})
  MATCH (b:DiabetesConcept {id: row.b})
  MERGE (a)-[r:HAS_SYMPTOM {source_id: source.id, fact_id: row.fact_id}]->(b)
  SET r += row, r.a = null, r.b = null, r.fact_id = row.fact_id
  RETURN count(*) AS rel_count_2
}
