    {a: "diabetes", b: "age_standardized_mortality_rates", fact_id: "8dbdeaf28903", section: "trang-13", evidence: "Between 2000 and 2019, there was an 8% increase in age-standardized mortality rates from diabetes (3)."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "cancers", fact_id: "405242af6fb8", section: "trang-13", evidence: "By contrast, the risk of dying from any one of the four main noncommunicable diseases (NCDs) (i.e. cardiovascular diseases, cancers, chronic respiratory diseases or diabetes) between the ages of 30 and 70 decreased by 20% globally in the same period (3)."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "lower_middle_income_countries", fact_id: "0126a476fd3d", section: "trang-13", evidence: "In lower middle-income countries, the mortality rate due to diabetes increased by 33% (3)."},
    {a: "diabetes", b: "physical_inactivity", fact_id: "da7fd56313b2", section: "trang-13", evidence: "These targets build on the global NCD targets established in 2013 (9), which include the target on ‘halt the rise in diabetes’ through monitoring prevalence of raised blood glucose/diabetes based on fasting plasma glucose (FPG) or medication for raised blood glucose, as well as specific targets for diabetes-related risk factors such as physical inactivity, tobacco use, obesity and hypertension."},
